  "prefLabel": "En 302.21 Register constant",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 302.21 “Register constant” means the factor by which the register reading is multiplied to convert the displayed register readings in kilowatt hours or other units taking into consideration the watt-hour constant, gear ratios, electronic register programming constants, and instrument transformer ratios as necessary. This term includes “dial constant,” “register multiplier,” or “reading multiplier.”\n\nSource. #14101, eff 10-22-24, EXPIRES: 10-22-34 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 300)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en300.html"
